    "note": "Raw export pulled via Figma MCP get_variable_defs across multiple nodes in both files, then merged by hand. Each get_variable_defs call returns values already resolved for whichever mode is active on that node, not the full mode matrix — so 'brands' below holds one resolved color/typography state per brand, not a true Brand x Theme grid. 'primitives' and 'typeScale' come from the UI-Components file and read as shared/global scales (font-size, spacing, radius, stroke, effects, grid) rather than brand-specific — radius and stroke values were only ever resolved on Gatlinburg-colored nodes (no Boyne-specific node captured yet), so per instruction they're applied across both brands for now. Font family/weight per role lives in brands.*.typography (confirmed clean per-brand); typeScale below only carries size/lineHeight/letterSpacing, since one source node resolved a mixed set of families that didn't cleanly match either brand.",
